> Tamaskan Dog Register Forum • View topic - Hello from Cardiff!
Hi everyone, I recently emailed Lynn and Jennie about a Tamaskan puppy and was directed here.
I've been looking for an ideal dog for around a year now, and been through many breeds so far that I haven't 'clicked' with. Among other things I like large, active, primitive, and strong-bonding dogs, and it's been hard to find a breed that encompasses all of these. Hoping my search is over now, lol. My girlfriend and I are moving around[ June]/July and planning to get her a dog soon after (an adult rescue), but I'm willing to wait a while for a Tam, they look perfect.[
]Are there any Tamaskan owners in or near[ Cardiff] we could chat to?[
]I don[�]�t live near you, I[�]�m in Scotland but I wanted to welcome you to the forum and also say you couldn[�]�t pick a better breed of dog for your wish list of your perfect breed[ ....]I currently have 3 having had one for nearly 12 years previously and I wouldn[�]�t have any other breed now[ ....]I notice you say you plan on getting your girlfriend an adult rescue dog[ ..]...have you considered rescuing or rehoming an adult Tamaskan?
